---
// Personal science — FDR-validated correlations + personal cutoffs. §1 calls this
// "a rigor most consumer apps don't attempt." The caffeine-cutoff example is from §1.
---

<section id="personal" class="scroll-mt-20 border-t border-line bg-sunk/40 py-20 md:py-28">
  <div class="shell grid items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow rise">Personal science</p>
      <h2 class="rise mt-4 text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.9rem)]">
        Findings from <span class="italic text-accent-soft">your</span> data &mdash; corrected for
        chance.
      </h2>
      <p class="rise mt-6 text-lg text-ink-soft">
        Robust per-metric baselines (median &plusmn; MAD), anomaly flags, and correlations tested
        with Spearman and Mann&ndash;Whitney under Benjamini&ndash;Hochberg FDR control &mdash; so a
        &ldquo;finding&rdquo; has survived the multiple-comparisons problem, not just caught your
        eye on a chart.
      </p>
      <p class="rise mt-5 text-[0.95rem] text-ink-faint">
        It&rsquo;s a rigor most consumer apps don&rsquo;t attempt. Detection is free, shown as plain
        statistics; the coach that explains and acts on it is the premium layer.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rise">
      <figure class="surface p-6 sm:p-7" aria-label="Example: a false-discovery-rate-controlled personal finding">
        <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
          <span class="eyebrow">Personal finding &middot; validated</span>
          <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">FDR-controlled</span>
        </figcaption>
        <hr class="hairline my-5" />
        <p class="font-serif text-[1.65rem] leading-snug">
          Caffeine after <span class="mono">~15:00</span>
          <span class="text-ink-faint">&rarr;</span>
          <span class="text-warn">&minus;40 min</span> sleep
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          On nights you logged a late coffee, you slept about 40 minutes less. Tested against your
          own baseline &mdash; a pattern in your data, never a population average pinned onto you.
        </p>
        <dl class="mono mt-5 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1.5 text-xs text-ink-faint">
          <dt>test</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Mann&ndash;Whitney, BH-corrected</dd>
          <dt>window</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">60 days</dd>
          <dt>holds</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">after correcting for chance</dd>
        </dl>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
